memory-map (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Much smaller downloads. Windows gets a zip of three files, 35 MB
    unpacked (0.4.1's program was 97 MB); keep them in one folder. The
    Linux packages are about a third of their old size.
  * Other Linux systems get a .tar.gz with the program and its two
    libraries in one folder, instead of a single large file.

